{
  "families": [
    {
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 11, "high": 18, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 8, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -2, "high": 2, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]},
        {"param": "m", "low": 2, "high": 8, "choices": null}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.7,
      "why": "pipelined_m is the most promising family for the area objective: it keeps 1 result/cycle but registers only every m stages, so increasing m directly reduces FF count. The spec's throughput constraint is only 1 MSPS, which is far below the Fmax of any plausible Artix-7 CORDIC stage, so trading Fmax for area via larger m should be beneficial. The m range 2..8 spans the area/Fmax trade-off; m=2 is close to fully pipelined, m=8 minimises registers. The accuracy parameters are searched over the same subspace as pipelined so that equal-accuracy points can be compared directly."
    },
    {
      "family": "pipelined",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 11, "high": 18, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 8, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -2, "high": 2, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.3,
      "why": "pipelined is the fully registered reference for the 1-result/cycle class. It will have the highest Fmax but also the highest FF count, so it is unlikely to win on luts_plus_ffs. It is included to (a) provide a baseline on the accuracy-area front, (b) cover cases where pipelined_m with large m might fail the 1 MSPS throughput constraint, and (c) confirm whether any accuracy level is reachable only with full pipelining. The accuracy parameter ranges match pipelined_m so that the two families can be compared at identical accuracy settings."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The binding constraint is max_abs_err <= 2^-10, while throughput >= 1 MSPS is trivial for any 1-result/cycle architecture on Artix-7. Therefore the search should focus on the area-accuracy trade-off. Accuracy depends only on data_width, n_iter, angle_guard, frac_guard and rounding, so both families are given the same accuracy ranges. data_width starts at 11 because the output LSB is 2^-(W-2); W=11 gives 0.5 LSB = 2^-10, the exact error limit, so W=12+ is likely needed but W=11 is kept to test the boundary. n_iter 8..20 covers the CORDIC angle-approximation error, with the lower end probing the minimum feasible iteration count. angle_guard -2..2 and frac_guard 0..3 focus on small guard widths that minimise area while still allowing enough internal precision. Both rounding modes are included because rounding can improve accuracy at no area cost. pipelined_m receives 70% of the budget because its m parameter gives a direct area/Fmax knob and it is expected to dominate the Pareto front; pipelined receives 30% as a reference and fallback. The ranges are deliberately wide enough to map the front but narrow enough to spend most evaluations near the feasible area-optimal region."
}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "next_plan": null,
  "rationale": "Final round reached, and the spec is feasible: 32/60 evaluations were feasible and the reported Pareto front contains 5 feasible designs. Both constraints are met on the front: throughput_msps is at least 65.4 (constraint >= 1) and max_abs_err is at most 0.000744 (2^-10.39), which satisfies <= 0.000976562. The area objective is already below the HV reference: best feasible luts_plus_ffs=1068 vs HV ref 1500, with the front covering luts_plus_ffs 1068..1308 and accuracy_bits 10.4..13.2 (HV ref 10). The spec's selection rule min luts_plus_ffs would pick the pipelined_m design [data_width=15, n_iter=16, angle_guard=0, frac_guard=1, rounding=round, m=6] at luts_plus_ffs=1068, accuracy_bits=10.4, max_abs_err=0.000744, throughput_msps=68.5. Since the final round is here and no constraint is unreachable, the correct decision is stop."
}
